Z||000000||ig88vsbobafett||12-28-2001||04:16 PM||||Hi i was going down the highway the other day and i took an exit and pushed the cluch in ans put  it in 2nd and there was a pop sound and now i cant go in any gear and it sounds like theres someing bouncing in side the tranny  (Its a 84 2m4 4 speed) ||||reg||1
Z||000001||West Coast Fiero||12-28-2001||04:27 PM||||it is highly probable that the shift finger bolt has snapped of the shift shaft, the bolt has now been spun around inside the trans, wearing down teeth and bearings. This is a common problem among 4 speeds, at least that I have seen and dealt with<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif"> <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000002||ig88vsbobafett||12-28-2001||04:36 PM||||Ok where can i look to see if that is it <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||West Coast Fiero||12-28-2001||04:45 PM||||take the shift shaft and try pulling it away from the transmission ( shaft with a lever that cable attaches to, lever moves for and aft ) if it comes out of the transmission than my usumption is correct<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif"> <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000004||ig88vsbobafett||12-28-2001||06:27 PM||||OK one more thing where can i get the parts i need to fix it and how much do they run <P>(It dose whats it said it would)<BR>(And how hard is it to fix) I plan on droping the moter to reseal it so thats not a problem||||reg||1
Z||000005||West Coast Fiero||12-28-2001||07:41 PM||||I have every internal part for the 4 speed, in fact its actually funny that you ask as I was cleaning the cabinets this morning I came across the box holding these parts.<P>I would rather sell all the parts at once rather than split it all up, infact I also happen to have a 4:10 final drive gear set if you are interested.<P> BUT - check out your RPO tag in the front compartment driver side, if you have the option MY8, then I would be willing to trade - send me your trans, I rebuild it with new refurbished parts, and I keep the old internals - thats it<P> The reason I do this is because you have a 3:32 gearset ( if you have the option code ) if you do not have this code then you have the more common 3:73 - I would like to keep your 3:32 set as payment and supply you with either a 4:10 or 3:73<P> its up to you, think it over<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif"> <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000006||ig88vsbobafett||12-28-2001||07:54 PM||||Is the RPO Tag the one on the drivers door ??||||reg||1
Z||000007||mrfiero||12-28-2001||08:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by West Coast Fiero:<BR><B>The reason I do this is because you have a 3:32 gearset ( if you have the option code ) if you do not have this code then you have the more common 3:73 - I would like to keep your 3:32 set as payment and supply you with either a 4:10 or 3:73<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Where do you get a 3.73 ratio from?  The only two ratios available on '84 Fieros w/4-speeds were the 3.32 and the 4.10.<P>Enlighten me.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||mrfiero||12-28-2001||08:12 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ig88vsbobafett:<BR><B>Is the RPO Tag the one on the drivers door ??</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No.  It's the rectangular tag on the inner fender well (under hood).<P>You are looking for either an MY8 or M19.<P>MY8=3.32 ratio and M19=4.10 ratio.<P>The odds are good you have the 4.10......almost all '84 4-speeds were the 4.10.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||West Coast Fiero||12-28-2001||08:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrfiero:<BR><B> <BR>Where do you get a 3.73 ratio from?  The only two ratios available on '84 Fieros w/4-speeds were the 3.32 and the 4.10.<P>Enlighten me.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>yup - your right, 3:73 is no such thing - I meant 3:63, which yes, was not available in 84<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif"> <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
